      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 5.11,
          "en": "So let's start with logging the user out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.11,
          "end": 6.49,
          "en": "and clearing the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.49,
          "end": 11,
          "en": "For that and the log out action besides committing this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11,
          "end": 13.74,
          "en": "we should also reach out to local storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.74,
          "end": 18.74,
          "en": "and remove the token and all the remove the user ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.38,
          "end": 22.25,
          "en": "Now that was the easy part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.25,
          "end": 26.13,
          "en": "The more tricky part is that we wanna log the user out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.13,
          "end": 28.483,
          "en": "automatically if the token expired.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.35,
          "end": 31.58,
          "en": "And for that got this token expiration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.58,
          "end": 34.863,
          "en": "which we aren't really using at the moment though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.81,
          "end": 37.44,
          "en": "Now when we do log in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.35,
          "end": 41.97,
          "en": "here like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.97,
          "end": 45.41,
          "en": "in the data which we get back from Firebase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.41,
          "end": 49.13,
          "en": "as you see in their docs, we also get the expires in field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.13,
          "end": 52.69,
          "en": "which is a text, but actually holds the number of seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.69,
          "end": 55.35,
          "en": "in which the ID token expires.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.35,
          "end": 59.28,
          "en": "I can tell you by default, that will be 3,600 seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.28,
          "end": 60.483,
          "en": "which is an hour.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.38,
          "end": 64.2,
          "en": "Now we wanna store that expiration date,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.2,
          "end": 67.09,
          "en": "not the duration because that doesn't help us,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.09,
          "end": 68.61,
          "en": "but the expiration date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.61,
          "end": 71.56,
          "en": "in the future when the token becomes invalid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.56,
          "end": 74.72,
          "en": "whenever we do log the user in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.72,
          "end": 79.72,
          "en": "So here in our off action, where we sent the request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.52,
          "end": 83.27,
          "en": "when we store that data in local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.27,
          "end": 88.27,
          "en": "we now also wanna derive the expiration date,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.44,
          "end": 91.69,
          "en": "which has a date in the future, which is the current date,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.69,
          "end": 95.363,
          "en": "plus the amount of seconds until the token expires.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.61,
          "end": 100.28,
          "en": "So for that we can get the current date by calling new date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.28,
          "end": 102.7,
          "en": "that gives us the current timestamp.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.7,
          "end": 107.49000000000001,
          "en": "But now I wanna add something here and actually for that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.49000000000001,
          "end": 109.3,
          "en": "I will call get time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.3,
          "end": 113.321,
          "en": "to get the current timestamp in milliseconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.321,
          "end": 115.93,
          "en": "and I wanna add the expiration time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.93,
          "end": 118.71000000000001,
          "en": "the expiration duration in milliseconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.71000000000001,
          "end": 120.97,
          "en": "So for that I'll add expires in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.79,
          "end": 127.79,
          "en": "and get that from responseData.expiresIn times 1,000",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 130.335,
          "end": 132.68,
          "en": "and ensure that this is converted to a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 132.68,
          "end": 134.77,
          "en": "by adding a plus here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 134.77,
          "end": 137.01,
          "en": "So that is then converting the string to a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.01,
          "end": 140.98,
          "en": "then since this is in seconds, I multiplied with 1,000",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.98,
          "end": 142.81,
          "en": "to have it in milliseconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 142.81,
          "end": 147.61,
          "en": "and then I can add expires in here to expiration dates,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.61,
          "end": 152.32999999999998,
          "en": "to have a new expiration timestamp in milliseconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 152.32999999999998,
          "end": 153.85,
          "en": "which will be in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.85,
          "end": 156.293,
          "en": "Current time plus that duration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.86,
          "end": 159.67000000000002,
          "en": "And it's this expiration date,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.67000000000002,
          "end": 163.46,
          "en": "which now also has to be stored in local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 163.46,
          "end": 168.46,
          "en": "So here I set a new item, which is the expiration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 169.04,
          "end": 171.35,
          "en": "which is called token expiration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 171.35,
          "end": 174.543,
          "en": "which is that expiration date.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 178.2,
          "end": 183.2,
          "en": "And here we now also store data in UX the expiration date.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 184.92,
          "end": 187.8,
          "en": "Actually, we don't even need it in UX",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 187.8,
          "end": 189.82,
          "en": "because local storage is enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 189.82,
          "end": 192.97,
          "en": "It only matters to us when we reload the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 192.97,
          "end": 196.32999999999998,
          "en": "So we don't need to commit it here and then in mutation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 196.32999999999998,
          "end": 198.29,
          "en": "we can actually also get rid of it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 201.9,
          "end": 206.253,
          "en": "And in try log in we also don't need to set this anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 207.4,
          "end": 210.43,
          "en": "Instead now we store it in local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 210.43,
          "end": 213.53,
          "en": "but I wanna do one other key thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 213.53,
          "end": 217.23,
          "en": "I wanna set a timer whenever the user is logged in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 217.23,
          "end": 219.55,
          "en": "so that we automatically log user out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 219.55,
          "end": 222.02,
          "en": "if that timer expires.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 222.02,
          "end": 223.81,
          "en": "And that's something that we'll also do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 223.81,
          "end": 225.453,
          "en": "in the auth actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 226.3,
          "end": 231.3,
          "en": "I will set a new time out here where I have my expires in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 231.98,
          "end": 235.47,
          "en": "so this time in milliseconds as a duration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 235.47,
          "end": 239.69,
          "en": "and after that duration, this function will execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 239.69,
          "end": 241.253,
          "en": "And in this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 242.45,
          "end": 245.62,
          "en": "I will simply dispatch the log out action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 245.62,
          "end": 249.363,
          "en": "because that's what I wanna do if the token expires.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 250.73,
          "end": 255.07,
          "en": "I also wanna make sure that I only have one timer active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 255.07,
          "end": 260.07,
          "en": "at a time so I will actually add a global variable here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 260.37,
          "end": 265.37,
          "en": "timer, which I use to hold my timer like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 268.85,
          "end": 270.7,
          "en": "and then we can use this timer variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 270.7,
          "end": 273.76,
          "en": "from anywhere in this file to clear the timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 273.76,
          "end": 276,
          "en": "And I wanna clear it whenever we log out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 276,
          "end": 279.23,
          "en": "When we log out, I wanna call clear timeout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 279.23,
          "end": 281.44,
          "en": "and pass this timer variable to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 281.44,
          "end": 283.77,
          "en": "to clear the ongoing timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 283.77,
          "end": 287.23,
          "en": "For example, if we manually clicked the log out button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 287.23,
          "end": 290.223,
          "en": "then I also wanna clear the log out timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 291.22,
          "end": 296.22,
          "en": "I also of course, wanna remove the token expiration item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 297.61,
          "end": 300.503,
          "en": "from local storage if we do log out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 303.15,
          "end": 305.47,
          "en": "And also not commit to this anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 305.47,
          "end": 309.083,
          "en": "because we don't store token expiration in Vuex anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 310.81,
          "end": 315.033,
          "en": "So now we've got this timer set whenever we logged in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 316.93,
          "end": 320.92,
          "en": "we also need to set this timer when we automatically log in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 320.92,
          "end": 325.03,
          "en": "then we need to check how much expiration time is left",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 325.03,
          "end": 328.26,
          "en": "and set a new timer to that time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 328.26,
          "end": 331.7,
          "en": "So that's why I'm storing token expiration in local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 331.7,
          "end": 334.26,
          "en": "So here I can get my token expiration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 334.26,
          "end": 339.26,
          "en": "by accessing local storage get item token expiration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 340.75,
          "end": 344.06,
          "en": "and that will now be a timestamp in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 344.06,
          "end": 345.81,
          "en": "So we now need to get to the difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 345.81,
          "end": 348.58299999999997,
          "en": "between that timestamp and the current time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 350.42,
          "end": 354.08299999999997,
          "en": "which I'll again store in a constant named expiresIn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 355.33,
          "end": 359.63,
          "en": "which is that token expiration converted to a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 359.63,
          "end": 364.63,
          "en": "by adding a plus minus to current time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 364.75,
          "end": 367.74,
          "en": "as a timestamp in milliseconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 367.74,
          "end": 370.34,
          "en": "So that will then be the difference in milliseconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 370.34,
          "end": 373.25,
          "en": "between this time and a future when the token expires",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 373.25,
          "end": 374.403,
          "en": "and the current time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 376.25,
          "end": 380.84,
          "en": "And of course, if expires in, should be negative here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 380.84,
          "end": 383.18,
          "en": "then we don't even need to log the user in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 383.18,
          "end": 387.63,
          "en": "We could even argue that if it's smaller than let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 387.63,
          "end": 390.94,
          "en": "10,000 so smaller than 10 seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 390.94,
          "end": 394.64,
          "en": "that even then logging the user in makes no sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 394.64,
          "end": 397.28,
          "en": "But I will go with smaller zero here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 397.28,
          "end": 399.79,
          "en": "And if expires in a smaller than that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 399.79,
          "end": 402.96,
          "en": "then the token is definitely invalid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 402.96,
          "end": 406.6,
          "en": "so then in that case, I will just return here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 406.6,
          "end": 410.15,
          "en": "and not continue with logging the user in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 410.15,
          "end": 412.11,
          "en": "because the timer expired,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 412.11,
          "end": 414.948,
          "en": "there is no need to continue here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 414.948,
          "end": 418.28,
          "en": "Otherwise though, if the timer is positive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 418.28,
          "end": 422.36,
          "en": "if we have enough time left, if the token is still valid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 422.36,
          "end": 427.36,
          "en": "I again will set a timer here with expiresIn as a duration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 427.95,
          "end": 430.89,
          "en": "and just as on my average timer in this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 430.89,
          "end": 435.49,
          "en": "I'll call context dispatch log out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 435.49,
          "end": 438.14300000000003,
          "en": "and store that timer in the timer variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 441.27,
          "end": 445.01,
          "en": "Okay, so theoretically that should work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 445.01,
          "end": 447.07,
          "en": "In order to test it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 447.07,
          "end": 450.75,
          "en": "I will manually tweak this expiration time a bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 450.75,
          "end": 452.15999999999997,
          "en": "and when we log in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 452.15999999999997,
          "end": 457.15999999999997,
          "en": "I will not set it to the actual exploration duration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 457.71,
          "end": 458.69,
          "en": "which we have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 458.69,
          "end": 460.19,
          "en": "But instead I'll duplicate this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 460.19,
          "end": 461.94,
          "en": "and comment out to the correct one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 461.94,
          "end": 465.19,
          "en": "and just set it to five seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 465.19,
          "end": 467.883,
          "en": "So now after five seconds, we should be logged out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 469.86,
          "end": 473.773,
          "en": "So if we give this a try and reload and log in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
